      "content": "I know exactly what you mean—when rest feels like a pause on a path to nowhere, it’s hard to see the point. But that zero-sum feeling is often a sign of deep burnout, not an objective truth about your worth. You don’t have to solve the meaning of life today; just try to notice one small thing that feels less heavy, even for a second. And if that feels impossible, please reach out to someone who can sit with you in that darkness—you don’t have to carry it alone.",
